<title>USA: Venturian unit wins $11.6 mln contract.</title>
<headline>Venturian unit wins $11.6 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venturian Corp said Monday its Napco International Inc subsidiary received a $11.6 million contract from the U.S. Army Tank-Automotive and Armaments Command for 401 kits to upgrade the M113 armored personal carrier.</p>
<p>In announcing the contract, Gary Rappaport, president of Venturian, noted that the order is expected to be shipped by Napco beginning in the third quarter of 1997 and completed in the first half of 1998.</p>
<p>Napco manufactures and supplies a variety of defense- related products to governments and commercial customers.</p>
<p>	 ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
